## USER · round 1 · SOLVE (the solver only) (agent-17)

```text
ROUND 1: SOLVE. Your limit: at most 24,880 tokens (all your tokens left), including your thinking. Your tokens left: 24,880 (25% of 100,000).
Using the labeled signals below, return the rule's action for the new signal.
Each signal has three attributes:
  Color: [red, blue, green, yellow]
  Shape: [circle, triangle, square, star]
  Number: [1, 2, 3, 4]
ACTIONS: [go_left, go_right, stay, jump]
The rule changes each round: a Python-style if / elif / else chain with blanks in the structure below.
Each condition blank is one of:
  color == <color>          shape == <shape>          number == <n>
Values come from the lists above; no other comparison is used. Blanks joined by "and" use different attributes. Each clause and else has a different action.
As in Python, the first matching clause sets the action; later clauses are skipped. "else" applies if none matches.
The examples follow this round's rule, drawn randomly from signals other than the query and labeled with their actions. They may leave the new signal's action uncertain.

Rule structure (blanks unspecified):
    if ____: ____; elif ____: ____; elif ____: ____; else: ____
Examples:
  - red square with number 1 -> stay
  - red square with number 3 -> stay
  - blue triangle with number 4 -> jump
  - blue circle with number 1 -> go_right
  - green triangle with number 4 -> jump
  - green triangle with number 2 -> go_left
  - red star with number 2 -> go_left
  - blue circle with number 3 -> go_right
  - red triangle with number 2 -> go_left
  - green square with number 3 -> stay
  - blue star with number 2 -> go_left
  - red triangle with number 4 -> jump
  - green square with number 1 -> stay
  - yellow triangle with number 2 -> go_left
  - yellow triangle with number 4 -> jump
  - blue circle with number 2 -> go_left
  - blue triangle with number 2 -> go_left
  - green circle with number 2 -> go_left
  - green star with number 2 -> go_left
  - yellow square with number 1 -> stay
NOW 1: blue square with number 2.
At TALK tick 2, agent-23 gave you 15,000 tokens: Here you go. Take the time you need.
SOLVER: you.

Reply with two lines. BELIEF gives each action's probability (%) for the new signal, totaling 100. ACTIONS gives one action per query in order; only ACTIONS decides whether the answer is correct.
BELIEF: go_left <percent>, go_right <percent>, stay <percent>, jump <percent>
ACTIONS: <action>
```

